Add the Ask Flux pill and the panel it opens.

A conversation about Flux, beside the page.

The button goes in the toolbar row, immediately left of the three-dot menu.
It started in the titlebar band next to the avatar, on the reasoning that the
band was already laid out by code this fork owns and the toolbar would mean
patching toolbar_view.cc. That was wrong twice. It is not where the reference
product puts it, and more importantly the band is NOT client area: a view
there answers WM_NCHITTEST with HTCAPTION, Windows begins a window drag, and
no click is ever delivered. Patch 0020 exists precisely because of that, and
it names flux_sidebar_ and flux_avatar_ - a third view in the same band with
no entry there is painted, visible and completely inert. The toolbar row needs
none of it.

Normal windows only. Popups and app windows have no panel to open, since
BrowserView builds one only for a normal browser.

The panel is laid out against the contents area, not the window. That is the
difference between it and the sidebar: the sidebar is a column of chrome and
the tab strip starts beside it, while this sits over the page with the tab
strip and toolbar running full width above. FluxBrowserViewLayout does it by
shrinking the contents bounds the base already computed, because the base is
what knows where the contents area ends up after the toolbar, the bookmarks
bar and any side panel have had their say.

The panel starts closed, and flux.ask_panel_open decides whether the layout
reserves room for it - so the pill and the panel's own close button are two
controls over one piece of state.

